# Blog posts

## Short filenames

Use **super short** Jekyll slugs. Prefer 1–3 words, kebab-case. The date prefix stays.

```
# ❌ BAD
_posts/2026-09-07-reflecting-on-10-years-of-adulthood.md

# ✅ GOOD
_posts/2026-09-07-10-years.md
```

Examples of good slugs: `10-years`, `getting-fit`, `carousels`, `manual`, `jest`.

Match asset names to the slug when practical (`assets/blog/{slug}.*`, `assets/metadata/posts/{slug}-og.png`).

## When the post is done → OG screenshot

When the user says they're done with a post (or ready to publish / ship / finalize), **capture the OG image** without waiting to be asked:

1. Confirm Jekyll is serving the post (`/{category}/{slug}.html`, usually `/en/{slug}.html`)
2. Run: `node scripts/capture-og.mjs /en/{slug}.html posts/{slug}-og`
3. Set front matter: `banner: /assets/metadata/posts/{slug}-og.png`

Details and edge cases (case studies, batch scripts): see `.cursor/rules/open-graph-images.mdc`.
